t\t\t\t\t>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tFact Sheets\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<li class=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tclass=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-link is-current\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\thref=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/releases/\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\taria-label=\"Releases\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tReleases\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<li class=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tclass=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-link\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\thref=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/remarks/\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\taria-label=\"Remarks\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tRemarks\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<li class=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tclass=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-link\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\thref=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/research/\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\taria-label=\"Research\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tResearch\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</ul>\n\t\t</div>\n\t</nav>\n\t</div>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Today, President Donald J. Trump returns to the Grand Canyon State for a visit to Bullhead City.</strong> He arrives with a clear record of America First results that put Arizona workers, families, seniors, and communities first — delivering tax relief, unleashing major private investment, ending the Biden-era border crisis, driving down violent crime, and securing Arizona’s critical water resources.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading has-text-align-center\" id=\"h-delivering-tax-relief-for-hardworking-arizonans\"><strong>Delivering Tax Relief for Hardworking Arizonans</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-text-align-center wp-block-paragraph\"><em>President Trump’s Working Families Tax Cuts are delivering direct relief to Arizona workers, families, and seniors.</em></p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>No Tax on Social Security:</strong>&nbsp;Approximately 1.3 million Arizona seniors&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Arizona-WH-OBBB-Savings-by-State.pdf\">benefit</a>&nbsp;from the new senior deduction.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Bigger Refunds:</strong>&nbsp;Arizona taxpayers saw average refunds of <a href=\"https://upgradedpoints.com/news/average-tax-refunds-by-state-county/\">$3,659</a> in 2026.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Rural Health Investments:</strong>&nbsp;Arizona&nbsp;<a href=\"https://scdailygazette.com/2025/12/30/sc-to-receive-200m-in-first-rural-hospital-funding-allocation/\">secured</a>&nbsp;$167 million in first-year Rural Health Transformation Program funding.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Protecting Jobs and Wages:</strong>&nbsp;The Working Families Tax Cuts&nbsp;<a href=\"https://nam.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/NAM_Tax_Wins_Collection_Final.pdf#page=5\">safeguarded</a>&nbsp;119,000 Arizona jobs, $22 billion in state GDP, and $11 billion in workers’ wages.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading has-text-align-center\" id=\"h-unleashing-an-investment-boom-in-arizona\"><strong>Unleashing an Investment Boom in Arizona</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-text-align-center wp-block-paragraph\"><em>President Trump’s agenda of tax cuts, energy dominance, secure borders, and pro-growth policies has attracted major private capital and high-quality jobs to Arizona.</em></p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Taiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing Company is <a href=\"https://www.enr.com/articles/63349-tsmc-arizona-megaproject-grows-to-265-billion\">expanding</a> advanced semiconductor manufacturing at its Phoenix facility with a $200 billion investment.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>EVelution Energy is <a href=\"https://kyma.com/news/top-stories/2026/05/19/cobalt-facility-planned-for-yuma-county-moves-forward/\">building</a> an $850 million cobalt processing facility in Yuma County, creating 3,300 jobs.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Amkor Technology is <a href=\"https://www.plantservices.com/industry-news/news/55314765/amkor-technology-invests-2-billion-to-build-semiconductor-manufacturing-facility-in-arizona\">constructing</a> a $2 billion semiconductor packaging and test facility in Peoria, creating 2,200 jobs.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Hadrian is <a href=\"https://www.gpec.org/news/press-releases/hadrian-announces-mesa-manufacturing-software-hub/\">establishing</a> a $200 million large-scale manufacturing and software hub in Mesa, creating 350 jobs.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Cyclic Materials is <a href=\"https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20250423172110/en/Cyclic-Materials-to-Invest-Over-USD-%2420M-in-its-First-Commercial-Facility-in-the-United-States\">developing</a> its first $20 million commercial facility in Mesa.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading has-text-align-center\" id=\"h-securing-the-southern-border\"><strong>Securing the Southern Border</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-text-align-center wp-block-paragraph\"><em>President Trump ended the Biden-era border crisis and restored control at the southern border.</em></p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>The Trump Administration <a href=\"https://www.dhs.gov/news/2026/09/16/trump-administration-delivers-16-straight-months-zero-releases-border\">has not released</a> a single illegal alien into the country at the border for 16 consecutive months.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Southern border apprehensions in August were <a href=\"https://www.dhs.gov/news/2026/09/16/trump-administration-delivers-16-straight-months-zero-releases-border\">94% lower</a> than the monthly average under Biden.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Refugee admissions in the first ten months of this fiscal year are <a href=\"https://www.pewresearch.org/short-reads/2026/08/17/refugee-admissions-to-the-us-are-dropping-sharply-in-trumps-second-term/#:~:text=The%20federal%20government%20has%20admitted%2010%2C258%20refugees%20through%20the%20first%2010%20months%20of%20fiscal%20year%202026%2C%20which%20ends%20on%20Sept.%2030.%20That%E2%80%99s%20down%20from%2038%2C102%20refugees%20in%20fiscal%202025%20and%20100%2C034%20in%20fiscal%202024.%20(President%20Joe%20Biden%20was%20in%20office%20for%20part%20of%20fiscal%202025%20and%20all%20of%20fiscal%202024.)\">down almost 90%</a> from 2024.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>The Working Families Tax Cuts <a href=\"https://www.judiciary.senate.gov/press/rep/releases/the-one-big-beautiful-bill-makes-america-safe-again\">allocated</a> $46.5 billion to complete the border wall.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Fentanyl and other drug trafficking are <a href=\"https://www.dhs.gov/news/2026/09/16/trump-administration-delivers-16-straight-months-zero-releases-border\">down</a>, with CBP seizing 73% more drugs this fiscal year through August than in the same period of FY 2024, and 61% more than the average for the same period over the prior four years.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>The Trump Administration <a href=\"https://www.doi.gov/pressreleases/department-interior-announces-land-transfer-department-navy-national-defense-arizona\">transferred</a> 285 acres of public land in Yuma County along the U.S.-Mexico border to the Department of the Navy to establish a National Defense Area in direct support of border security operations.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading has-text-align-center\" id=\"h-making-safer-streets-across-arizona\"><strong>Making Safer Streets Across Arizona</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-text-align-center wp-block-paragraph\"><em>Violent crime is falling as President Trump’s law-and-order agenda delivers real results for Arizona communities.</em></p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Violent crime <a href=\"https://azcrimestatistics.azdps.gov/tops/report/violent-crimes/arizona/2025\">fell</a> 13% statewide last year, including a 13% drop in homicides, an 11% drop in aggravated assaults, a 24% drop in robberies, and a 10% drop in sexual assaults.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>In Mesa, homicides <a href=\"https://majorcitieschiefs.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/MCCA-Violent-Crime-Report-2026-and-2025-Midyear.pdf\">fell</a> 33% and rapes fell 15% in the first half of this year compared with the same period last year.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>In Phoenix, homicides <a href=\"https://majorcitieschiefs.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/MCCA-Violent-Crime-Report-2026-and-2025-Midyear.pdf\">fell</a> 22% and robberies fell 19% in the first half of this year compared with the same period last year.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>In Tucson, homicides <a href=\"https://majorcitieschiefs.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/MCCA-Violent-Crime-Report-2026-and-2025-Midyear.pdf\">fell</a> 24% and robberies fell 10% in the first half of this year compared with the same period last year.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading has-text-align-center\" id=\"h-protecting-arizona-s-water-resources\"><strong>Protecting Arizona’s Water Resources</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-text-align-center wp-block-paragraph\"><em>The Trump Administration is making targeted investments to strengthen Arizona’s water supply and long-term resilience.</em></p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>In July 2025, the Bureau of Reclamation <a href=\"https://www.usbr.gov/newsroom/news-release/5202\">announced</a> a $179 million investment to design and construct the North Gateway Advanced Water Purification Facility in Phoenix.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>In May 2025, the Trump Administration <a href=\"https://www.doi.gov/pressreleases/interior-secures-18-short-term-agreements-boost-colorado-river-conservation\">finalized</a> 18 short-term System Conservation Implementation agreements with water entitlement holders in Arizona and California to increase conservation of Colorado River System water.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\" />\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>President Trump and Republicans are delivering America First policies that put Arizona first: lower taxes, major private investment, a secure border, safer communities, and critical water infrastructure.</strong> Arizonans face a clear choice between continuing this progress, or returning to the higher taxes, energy restrictions, and open borders policies of the past.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/releases/2026/10/president-trump-returns-to-arizona-with-a-record-of-results-tax-relief-jobs-and-border-security/\">President Trump Returns to Arizona with a Record of Results: Tax Relief, Jobs, and Border Security</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov\">The White House</a>.</p>",
